    "metadata": {
      "name": "EventGraph",
      "description": "Wall-clock time nodes: year, timestamp, ISO text and second arithmetic.",
      "version": "1.0.0",
      "created_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z",
      "modified_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z"
    },
    "comments": [
      {
        "id": "comment-1",
        "text": "DATE AND TIME\n\nTime nodes read the wall clock (Current Year, Current Hour, Unix Timestamp ...) and convert between\nunits. A timestamp is whole seconds since 1970-01-01 UTC, so arithmetic is plain integer maths:\nAdd Seconds, Hours To Seconds, Timestamp Difference. Format ISO / Format Human turn one into text.\n(Game time for gameplay is Get Delta Time and Delay; use these for real-world dates.)",
        "position": [
          60.0,
          -300.0
        ],
        "size": [
          900.0,
          200.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.2,
          0.4,
          0.8,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": []
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-2",
        "text": "THE CLOCK\nCurrent Year is stored, then Assert Greater Than checks it is later than 2023. Unix Timestamp -> Format ISO -> Print shows the current moment as text.",
        "position": [
          360.0,
          100.0
        ],
        "size": [
          1760.0,
          100.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.2,
          0.65,
          0.35,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": []
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-3",
        "text": "ARITHMETIC\nTimestamp 0 (1970) is in the past: true. 2 hours = 7200 seconds. 0 + 3600 = 3600.",
        "position": [
          2160.0,
          690.0
        ],
        "size": [
          1260.0,
          90.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.9,
          0.55,
          0.15,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": []
      }
    ],
